Partial tobacco products tax repeal. 25LSO-0739, 1.0
FISCAL NOTE
FY 2026 FY 2027 FY 2028
NON-ADMINISTRATIVE IMPACT
Anticipated Revenue (decrease)
GENERAL FUND ($6,700,000) ($6,700,000) ($6,700,000)
Source of revenue (decrease):
This bill repeals the state excise taxes on all tobacco products other than
cigarettes, including cigars, snuff, other tobacco products, electronic
cigarettes and vapor material. All excise taxes on these products are distributed
to the General Fund.
Assumptions:
According to the Department of Revenue 2024 Annual report, $6,727,052 was
collected in FY 2024 on excise taxes on all tobacco products other than
cigarettes.
It is assumed that revenues from all tobacco products other than cigarettes would
remain at FY 2024 levels in FY 2026 through FY 2028.
Any additional fiscal or personnel impact is not determinable due to insufficient
time to complete the fiscal note process.
